          "blocks": [
            {
              "label": "Direct workspace contribution 1",
              "before": "## Workspace display names\n\nMigration 004 adds `mly_workspace_profiles`, self-only alias writes, atomic named join/create wrappers and alias joins in existing contribution pages. `WorkspaceDisplayNameEditor.tsx` provides explicit profile management for owners and members. Names are unverified, scoped to a workspace and paired with short ID tags; all roles, card keys, note ownership, filters and writes remain UUID-based. Existing note versions never change when an alias changes. The profile setter accepts no target user ID, authenticated direct profile writes are forbidden, and current membership controls reads/renames. No per-hover/card profile requests or email disclosure. See `docs/WORKSPACE-DISPLAY-NAMES.md` for upgrade/retention/rollback guidance and tests.\n",
              "after": "## Workspace display names\n\nMigration 004 adds `mly_workspace_profiles`, self-only alias writes, atomic named join/create wrappers and alias joins in existing contribution pages. `WorkspaceDisplayNameEditor.tsx` provides explicit profile management for owners and members. Names are unverified, scoped to a workspace and paired with short ID tags; all roles, card keys, note ownership, filters and writes remain UUID-based. Existing note versions never change when an alias changes. The profile setter accepts no target user ID, authenticated direct profile writes are forbidden, and current membership controls reads/renames. No per-hover/card profile requests or email disclosure. See `docs/WORKSPACE-DISPLAY-NAMES.md` for upgrade/retention/rollback guidance and tests.\n\n## Direct creation and titles\n\nMigration 005 separates observation titles from workspace category assignments. `WorkspaceContributionDraft.tsx` owns an unsaved, per-workspace direct draft and stable retry identity. `WorkspaceLocationPicker.ts` owns one-shot map intent; the notes panel exposes the map temporarily and cancels cleanly, while runtime supplies only SDK coordinates/cursor/ripple adapters. Publication remains explicit, UUID-authorized and duplicate-safe. Local publication stays available as a secondary path with a workspace title/category. Legacy blank titles fall back to category headings. See `docs/DIRECT-WORKSPACE-CONTRIBUTIONS.md` for operator rollout, limits, code map and rollback.\n"
            }
          ]
